--   The child wrapper (round six, `cost_childH`)
-- statement:
--   **The child wrapper** overhead (constant child cost `cI`).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6IL3Cost`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.IL3H.cost_childH {c : IntMul.Kappa.R6.IL3H.Cfg} {W A m Bn t S0 r Z Zr H G DWc x cI : ℕ} (hW : 1 ≤ W)
--       (hZZ : Z ≤ Zr) (hS : 1 ≤ S0) (hBn : 1 ≤ Bn) (hsz : gsSz c + 6 ≤ A) (hGH : G ≤ H)
--       (hGZ : zsz (G : ℤ) ≤ Zr) (hZr : Zr + 2 ≤ r) (hx : x + (DWc + (G + 2) * W) ≤ H) :
--       cChF c Zr G + cWrapQ W (nN Bn t S0 * r) Z G DWc (fun _ => cI + 2) x +
--         (4 * (2 * (Zr + G + 1) + 2) + 1) ≤ cI + MlocH W A m * ((W * nN Bn t S0) * Yu r Zr H)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, item language (I3): cost bounds of the steps of a node
--
--   `KFWCost2` with the literal `W_c`, `A0`, `mC` replaced by variables: with
--   `P = (W n) · Yu r Z H` (`n` records per role, `W` roles, at most `A` atoms per gate, `m` slots):
--
--   * `cost_gateH`, `cost_permH`, `cost_phaseH`, `cost_fixGH`, `cost_rowH`: every local step costs
--     `≤ MlocH W A m · P` (plus the row body);
--   * `cost_childH`: the child wrapper adds `≤ MlocH W A m · P` to the (constant) child cost, for
--     `gsSz c + 6 ≤ A`.
--
